### Task 4 — Validity Audit

| Threat | Description | Control / Disclosure |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Hardware Heterogeneity** | CPU threads may share cache/memory bandwidth differently than the GPU's dedicated VRAM bandwidth. | Disclose specific CPU model, architecture (e.g., AVX-512 support), and GPU memory bandwidth. |
| **Driver/API Overhead** | Vulkan and CUDA have different kernel launch overheads and memory management behaviors. | Run "warm-up" iterations and report "steady-state" performance after the first 10 tokens. |
| **Quantization Parity** | Different backends may handle the same Q4_K_M weights using different kernels (e.g., GGML vs. specialized CUDA kernels). | Verify that the exact same model weights and quantization bit-depth are used across all tests. |
| **Workload Divergence** | **The CPU might be bottlenecked by memory bandwidth while the GPU is bottlenecked by compute (or vice versa) depending on sequence length.** | **Control:** Run tests at multiple sequence lengths (e.g., 128, 512, 2048) to identify the bottleneck point for each backend. |

